Per tower@0.5.3:

ServiceExt::oneshot takes self: Sized and returns Oneshot<Self, Request>. Its Future impl requires S: Service<Req> and yields type Output = Result<S::Response, S::Error>. The provided content does not include the Oneshot struct definition and does not indicate a Send bound on Self; thus, from this package the only exact trait bound is S: Service<Req>, and Send on Self is not specified here.

Source excerpt:
> // src/util/oneshot.rs
> impl<S, Req> Future for Oneshot<S, Req> where S: Service<Req>, {
>     type Output = Result<S::Response, S::Error>;
> 
>     fn poll(self: Pin<&mut Self>, cx: &mut Context<'_>) -> Poll<Self::Output>;
> }
